<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat futures stay strong.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat futures stay strong.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sydney Futures Exchange wheat remained strong on Friday with most settlement prices moving ahead by A$2.00 to A$5.00 a tonne.</p>
<p>Two contracts traded for a total market volume of four lots.</p>
<p>May 1997 rose by A$1.50 to A$181.00 a tonne on two lots traded while July 1997 edged back by A$1.50 to A$182.00.</p>
<p>The market was well-bid and reflected high cash prices in the physical market, Phil Lindsay of Ord Minnett Jardine Fleming Futures Ltd said.  </p>
